WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.364 --> 00:00:02.850
- [Narrator] Made entirely of
wood without a single nail,

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:05.291
the Sanctuary of Truth
in Pattaya, Thailand,

00:00:05.291 --> 00:00:06.878
is a modern-day marvel built

00:00:06.878 --> 00:00:09.628
using ancient carving techniques.

00:00:12.876 --> 00:00:15.192
This religious shrine has
been under construction

00:00:15.192 --> 00:00:16.491
since 1981,

00:00:16.491 --> 00:00:19.862
and it isn't scheduled to
be completed anytime soon.

00:00:19.862 --> 00:00:21.940
It was commissioned by a Thai millionaire,

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:25.394
who spent his fortune
on projects like this.

00:00:25.394 --> 00:00:28.929
He wanted to keep ancient
wood-building techniques alive.

00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:33.814
The building towers 375 feet,
and looks out over the coast.

00:00:33.814 --> 00:00:36.940
Its four wings are dedicated
to Thai, Cambodian,

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.785
Chinese, and Indian iconography.

00:00:39.785 --> 00:00:43.235
A team of 250 wood carvers
have created ornate images

00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:45.634
of religious and
philosophical significance

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:47.668
throughout the structure.

00:00:47.668 --> 00:00:50.633
The Sanctuary of Truth is
considered an art installation,

00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:54.129
religious shrine, and
cultural monument, all in one.

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:56.524
Although the creator has
passed away and won't have

00:00:56.524 --> 00:01:00.135
an opportunity to see his
celestial masterpiece completed,

00:01:00.135 --> 00:01:04.302
the work continues according
to his specific plans.

